  "Summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner known for completing marathons in a bionic suit after being paralysed in a riding accident, has died at the age of 44 following an accident in Jordan. Lomas, who lived in Melton, Leicestershire, began her charity work after a 2007 accident at the Osberton Horse Trials left her paralysed from the chest down. She gained fame for running the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit and was chosen to light the Paralympic cauldron that year. In 2016, she completed the Great North Run while pregnant, also wearing her bionic suit. Her family has requested privacy to grieve."
